},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":["W"],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Plains","oracle_id":"bc71ebf6-2056-41f7-be35-b2e5c34afa99","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {W}.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["W"],"released_at":"2026-11-13","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land — Plains"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["W"],"colors":["W"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{3}{W}{W}","name":"Tragic Arrogance","oracle_id":"8a29bd35-33ef-4317-9fe5-8aaff5d7d64d","oracle_text":"For each player, you choose from among the permanents that player controls an artifact, a creature, an enchantment, and a planeswalker. Then each player sacrifices all other nonland permanents they control.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"A permanent with more than one type may be chosen as either of the types or both. For example, an artifact creature may be chosen as the artifact, the creature, or both. Choosing the same permanent twice this way has the same result as choosing it once.","oracle_id":"2e4865c5-a590-4820-81ec-926014ddb8c4","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Cataclysmic Gearhulk will be sacrificed to its own ability if you don't choose it as your artifact or your creature.","oracle_id":"2e4865c5-a590-4820-81ec-926014ddb8c4","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"First the player whose turn it is chooses permanents they control, then each other player in turn order does the same. Each player will know the choices made by players who chose before them. All of the unchosen nonland permanents are then sacrificed simultaneously.","oracle_id":"2e4865c5-a590-4820-81ec-926014ddb8c4","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you don't control any permanents of one of the types, you'll still choose the permanents of the types you do control.","oracle_id":"2e4865c5-a590-4820-81ec-926014ddb8c4","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Lands can't be chosen and won't be sacrificed, even if they have other types (such as an artifact land).","oracle_id":"2e4865c5-a590-4820-81ec-926014ddb8c4","published_at":"2016-09-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a permanent has more than one of the affected types, it can count for any of them. For example, you could choose an artifact creature as the artifact you're sparing, another creature as the creature, and an enchantment creature as the enchantment. Similarly, you could choose an enchantment creature as both the creature and the enchantment that you're sparing, even if the player controls another creature and/or another enchantment.","oracle_id":"8a29bd35-33ef-4317-9fe5-8aaff5d7d64d","published_at":"2015-06-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"None of the chosen permanents are targets of Tragic Arrogance.","oracle_id":"8a29bd35-33ef-4317-9fe5-8aaff5d7d64d","published_at":"2015-06-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Although Darksteel Citadel is an artifact, it can't be cast as a spell. Playing it follows the normal rules for playing a land.","oracle_id":"8dc067bf-f78f-4ac4-b6e7-b305c42cf0bc","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you control a permanent with more than one type, you can choose that permanent to be the representative of either type. This makes it possible to have more than one creature (or other permanent type) on the battlefield. For example, if you select a creature for your creature and an artifact creature for your artifact, you get to keep both of these creatures.","oracle_id":"b0479ca4-e925-4aa7-a4fa-f7e01f899ac5","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you control a permanent with more than one type, you can choose that same permanent for more than one of the choices if you want to. This makes it possible to select an artifact creature as both your artifact and creature, and then select a land and thereby keep only two cards.","oracle_id":"b0479ca4-e925-4aa7-a4fa-f7e01f899ac5","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The current player makes their choices before the other player. After both players make choices, all the sacrifices are done simultaneously.","oracle_id":"b0479ca4-e925-4aa7-a4fa-f7e01f899ac5","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The permanents to save are chosen on resolution. You do not choose them when casting the spell.","oracle_id":"b0479ca4-e925-4aa7-a4fa-f7e01f899ac5","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each permanent not chosen by a player will be sacrificed. If a permanent has none of the listed types (for example, a Planeswalker with no other types), it can’t be chosen.","oracle_id":"b0479ca4-e925-4aa7-a4fa-f7e01f899ac5","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
